~~
    Module System Test

    `get path` compiles another .ct file in place. The path is relative
    to the importing file and `.ct` is optional. A module is loaded once,
    however many times it is imported.
    `get c:lib { ... }` declares C functions from a C library instead.
~~

get lib/mathx
get "lib/consts.ct"     ~ quotes are optional

get c:m {
    sqrt(x: double): double
}

write square(answer)
write sqrt(16.0)
